                                        "entry_id": "07d0ebbe-ed1e-30a0-9af5-bf97f9749cb6",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A function giving the change in the linear approximation of f at a point x over a small interval Δx or operatorname d!x, the function being called the differential of f and denoted operatorname d!f(x,Δx), operatorname d!f(x), or simply operatorname d!f."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "of a univariate differentiable function f(x)"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "92af5792-68ae-40f6-bbb5-a9c907bd7120",
                                                "sense_id": "e67955c3-739e-3ab1-b1d7-961367e713e8",
                                                "text": "If f(x)#61;x², the differential of f is the function #92;operatorname#123;d#125;#92;#33;f(x,#92;Deltax)#61;f'(x)#92;Deltax#61;2x#92;Deltax."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
